# Reduced motion
@scenario tutorial_lesson_29
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide neutral]
pip: Reduced motion keeps the same instructions and choices while omitting movement.
pip: Change the motion setting in the topic menu, then replay Character movement or Camera movement.
> Compare reduced motion -> preview_still
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label preview_still
[if tutorial_still]
pip: With reduced motion on, Pip uses a stationary pose.
[else]
[move pip guide stride-a-right exprdur=0]
[move pip rightmark ease_in_out_cubic 620]
[wait 150]
[move pip rightmark stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 150]
[move pip rightmark stride-c-right exprdur=0]
[wait 150]
[move pip rightmark stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 170]
[move pip rightmark point exprdur=90]
pip: With motion on, Pip walks across the stage and back.
[move pip rightmark stride-a-left exprdur=0]
[move pip guide ease_out_cubic 500]
[wait 120]
[move pip guide stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move pip guide stride-c-left exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move pip guide stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip guide neutral exprdur=90]
[endif]
[jump check]
@label check
pip: What must remain available in still mode?
> The same story and navigation. -> correct
> Only the title screen. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: Optional motion should never gate information or progress. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: Optional motion should never gate information or progress.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_29]
[flag tutorial_done_29]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_6]
